# Pairs with RLinearizedTerminals. When only one participant tree is replicated
# here and a decommission drops it before its terminal arrived, the barrier
# decides over the trees that remain - none - and so commits with no verdict to
# take. The tree, added back, then joins the decided barrier and is finalized
# committed though the operation aborted. Production never reaches a barrier
# with no arrival - the opening terminal's arrival is written with the wait
# set, and the drop refuses an arrived tree - and #4740's guard keeps it from
# deciding one (issue #4741).
MODULE: RLinearizedTerminalsBarrierDecidesWithNoArrival
TARGET: RLinearizedTerminals
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a barrier left with no tree to wait for decides committed over no arrival
PERTURBS: Decommission
BOUNDS: LossPath = 4, JoinStart = 0, SagaOutcome = 2, Shape = 1, PreHold = 0, DialFaults = 0, OneReplicated = 1

--- FIND
           complete == cdec = "inflight" /\ live # {} /\ \A w \in live : carr[w] # "none"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: an empty remainder decides.
           complete == cdec = "inflight" /\ \A w \in live : carr[w] # "none"
--- END
